      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and $det(A)=0$?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$ A\\text{ is invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\text{Col}(A)&=\\mathbb{R}^{4} \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)&=4 \\\\ \\text{Null}(A)&=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A)&=0\\end{aligned}\\right. $$\n\n$det(A)=0$, so $A$ is not invertible.\n\nWe have $\\text{rank}(A)<4$, $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$, $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne\\{0\\}$, and $\\text{Col}(A)\\ne\\mathbb{R}^{4}$.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $A\\text{ is invertible}$ is false. $A$ is not invertible.\n\n- Statement $\\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\}$ is false. $\\text{Null}(A)\\ne \\{0\\}$.\n\n- Statement $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$ is true. $\\text{nullity}(A)>0$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0$ only.",
